This license governs **this repository and the skill packages it builds** — the
skill definitions under `skills/`, the shared contracts under `shared/`, the
build and gate tooling, the tests, and the `.skill` bundles emitted into `dist/`.

It is the same license used across the author's other repositories, so a single
attribution form works for all of them.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

WHAT THIS FILE IS, AND WHAT `shared/licensing-and-credits.md` IS

These are two different things, and confusing them is the gap this file closes.

  THIS FILE          governs the skills themselves — the source you are reading
                     and the packages you may install.

  shared/licensing-  is a TEMPLATE the skills apply to the DOCUMENTS they help
  and-credits.md     you produce. Every value in it is a `{{profile}}`
                     placeholder filled in from your own project profile. It has
                     never licensed this repository, and it does not.

An everyday version: this file is the licence on the woodworking tools. That
file is the label the tools help you print for the furniture you build with
them. Owning the tools does not make the author of the tools the owner of your
furniture, and vice versa.

